---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Lay out the shards" hint="20,000 workspaces share 100 TB of data. Choose how many logical shards they are hashed into, how many physical databases hold those shards, and whether one workspace is enormous, then see how evenly the data spreads and how big the biggest unit is. A simple model with invented workspaces, not Notion's data.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Press <b>Reset</b>. With <b>Few, large logical shards</b> (32 of them) on <b>Thirty-two physical databases</b>, hashing workspaces to shards spreads the data well: the heaviest database holds <b>3.5</b> TB against an average of <b>3.1</b> TB, which is <b>1.1</b> times the average. With one logical shard on each database, the biggest unit is a whole database, <b>3.5</b> TB.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Logical shards</b> to <b>Many small logical shards</b>, which is 480: the databases hold the same data as before, <b>3.5</b> TB at the heaviest, but each now has <b>15</b> logical shards, and the biggest single shard falls to <b>0.6</b> TB, a unit small enough to move by itself.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Physical databases</b> to <b>Thirty-five physical databases</b>: 480 shards do not divide evenly, so each database holds <b>13 to 14</b> of them. The average is <b>2.9</b> TB and the heaviest database <b>3.3</b> TB, <b>1.2</b> times the average.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Physical databases</b> to <b>Forty physical databases</b>: now every database holds exactly <b>12</b> shards. The average falls to <b>2.5</b> TB and the heaviest is <b>2.9</b> TB. Because 480 divides evenly by 32, 40 and 48, the cluster can grow in even steps like this without splitting any shard.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Largest workspace</b> to <b>One workspace holds 5% of all the data</b>: the heaviest database jumps to <b>7.2</b> TB, <b>2.9</b> times the average, and the biggest logical shard is <b>5.1</b> TB. Every block belongs to one workspace, so that workspace cannot be split, and more logical shards would not help.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg nsh" data-nsh>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Logical shards <select class="pg-in" data-shards><option value="32">Few, large logical shards (32)</option><option value="96">A middling number of logical shards (96)</option><option value="480">Many small logical shards (480)</option></select></label>
      <label>Physical databases <select class="pg-in" data-databases><option value="32">Thirty-two physical databases</option><option value="35">Thirty-five physical databases</option><option value="40">Forty physical databases</option><option value="48">Forty-eight physical databases</option></select></label>
      <label>Largest workspace <select class="pg-in" data-big><option value="off">Workspaces of typical sizes</option><option value="on">One workspace holds 5% of all the data</option></select></label>
      <button type="button" class="btn" data-reset>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Heaviest database</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Heaviest compared with the average</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Biggest logical shard</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Logical shards on each database</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <svg class="nsh-chart" viewBox="0 0 600 130" role="img" data-chart preserveAspectRatio="none">
      <g data-bars></g>
      <line data-average-line x1="0" x2="600" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="5 4" />
    </svg>
    <p class="pg-note">One bar for each physical database: how much data it holds. The dashed line is the average.</p>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model, invented for teaching and not Notion data: 20,000 workspaces whose sizes follow a skewed curve, many small and a few large, add up to 100 TB. Each workspace ID is hashed to one logical shard, evenly across the shards, as Notion divides workspace UUIDs into uniform buckets. Neighbouring logical shards share a physical database. When the shards do not divide evenly over the databases, some databases get one more than the others. The enormous workspace holds 5% of all the data. Notion's real layout is 480 logical shards on 32 physical databases, 15 on each, but its post gives no workspace sizes, and real data is more complicated than this.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style>
  .nsh-chart { width: 100%; height: 130px; display: block; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; }
</style>
<script>
  import { query } from '../../playground';
  import { simulate } from '../../models/notion-sharding.ts';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-nsh]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const SVGNS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
    const CHART_WIDTH = 600, CHART_HEIGHT = 130, CHART_PAD = 8, BAR_GAP = 2;
    const CHART_HEADROOM = 1.1; // the tallest bar leaves a little room above
    const BAD_IMBALANCE = 1.5; // a heaviest database this many times the average turns the box red
    const DEFAULTS: Record<string, string> = { shards: '32', databases: '32', big: 'off' };
    const select = (key: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(`[data-${key}]`);
    const tb = (n: number) => `${n.toFixed(1)} TB`;

    function draw() {
      const result = simulate({ logicalShards: Number(select('shards').value), databases: Number(select('databases').value), bigWorkspace: select('big').value === 'on' });
      const { min, max } = result.logicalShardsPerDatabase;
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = tb(result.heaviestDatabaseTb);
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = `the average is ${tb(result.averageDatabaseTb)}`;
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${result.imbalance.toFixed(1)} times`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = result.imbalance > BAD_IMBALANCE ? 'one database carries far more than its share' : 'close to an even spread';
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = tb(result.heaviestLogicalShardTb);
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = 'the largest unit that would have to be moved as one piece';
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = min === max ? String(min) : `${min} to ${max}`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = min === max ? 'the same on every database' : 'the shards do not divide evenly over the databases';
      const bad = [result.imbalance > BAD_IMBALANCE, result.imbalance > BAD_IMBALANCE, result.heaviestLogicalShardTb > result.averageDatabaseTb, min !== max];
      ['b1', 'b2', 'b3', 'b4'].forEach((b, i) => q<HTMLElement>(`[data-${b}]`).style.setProperty('--c', bad[i] ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)'));

      const bars = q('[data-bars]'); bars.replaceChildren();
      const top = result.heaviestDatabaseTb * CHART_HEADROOM; const slot = CHART_WIDTH / result.databaseTb.length;
      const y = (v: number) => CHART_HEIGHT - CHART_PAD - (v / top) * (CHART_HEIGHT - 2 * CHART_PAD);
      result.databaseTb.forEach((v, i) => {
        const rect = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, 'rect');
        rect.setAttribute('x', (i * slot + BAR_GAP / 2).toFixed(1)); rect.setAttribute('width', (slot - BAR_GAP).toFixed(1));
        rect.setAttribute('y', y(v).toFixed(1)); rect.setAttribute('height', (CHART_HEIGHT - CHART_PAD - y(v)).toFixed(1));
        rect.setAttribute('fill', v === result.heaviestDatabaseTb ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--role-1)');
        bars.append(rect);
      });
      const line = q('[data-average-line]'); line.setAttribute('y1', y(result.averageDatabaseTb).toFixed(1)); line.setAttribute('y2', y(result.averageDatabaseTb).toFixed(1));
      q('[data-chart]').setAttribute('aria-label', `Data on each of ${result.databaseTb.length} databases, from ${tb(Math.min(...result.databaseTb))} to ${tb(result.heaviestDatabaseTb)}, average ${tb(result.averageDatabaseTb)}`);

      const out = q('[data-verdict]'); const uneven = min !== max; const skewed = result.imbalance > BAD_IMBALANCE;
      out.classList.toggle('bad', skewed || uneven);
      if (skewed) out.textContent = `The heaviest database holds ${tb(result.heaviestDatabaseTb)}, ${result.imbalance.toFixed(1)} times the average. A workspace is never split, so more shards cannot spread it: its shard alone is ${tb(result.heaviestLogicalShardTb)}.`;
      else if (uneven) out.textContent = `The data is spread well, but the shards do not divide evenly: some databases hold ${max} shards and some ${min}. Choose a shard count that divides evenly over the databases.`;
      else out.textContent = `Even: every database holds ${max} logical shard${max === 1 ? '' : 's'} and the heaviest holds ${tb(result.heaviestDatabaseTb)}, ${result.imbalance.toFixed(1)} times the average. The biggest logical shard is ${tb(result.heaviestLogicalShardTb)}.`;
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    q('[data-reset]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      Object.keys(DEFAULTS).forEach((k) => (select(k).value = DEFAULTS[k]));
      draw();
    });
    draw();
  });
</script>
